<article class="env-lemma" id="0CTQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CTQ">Lemma <span data-tag="0CTQ">76.51.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Consider a commutative diagram of algebraic spaces </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z' \ar[d] \ar[r] &  Y' \ar[d] \\  X' \ar[r] &  B' }  \]
</div>
  <p> over $S$. Let $B \to B'$ be a morphism. Denote by $X$ and $Y$ the base changes of $X'$ and $Y'$ to $B$. Assume $Y' \to B'$ and $Z' \to X'$ are flat. Then $X \times _ B Y$ and $Z'$ are Tor independent over $X' \times _{B'} Y'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/08IQ" data-tag="08IQ">75.20.3</a> we may check tor independence étale locally on $X \times _ B Y$ and $Z'$. This<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001472819" id="a0001472819-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> reduces the lemma to the case of schemes which is More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CTA" data-tag="0CTA">37.69.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>